---
title: "PDF Export - Columns"
enterprise: true
---

PDF export uses displayed columns in their current order. Set `allColumns=true` or provide `columnKeys` to export a different set. Set `exportRowNumbers=true` to include the Row Numbers column.

## Column Widths

The `columnWidth` option accepts:

- `'grid'` to use current grid widths.
- `'auto'` to size from exported content, which can keep columns such as Row Numbers compact.
- A number to use one width in points.
- A callback to configure each exported column.

By default, PDF export uses current grid widths for regular columns and sizes the Row Numbers column from its exported content.

Widths are proportionally reduced when their total exceeds the printable page width. Smaller tables are not stretched.

## Text Wrapping

Cells remain on one line by default. Set `wrapText=true` to wrap all cells and grow rows automatically. Existing `colDef.wrapText` and `colDef.wrapHeaderText` values are reused unless `skipStyleCallbacks=true`.

Use `PdfCellStyle.wrapText` through `currentElementStyleCallback` for PDF-specific row or column behaviour.

